A||N||3||V6pack||Dumb front suspension question||||5||
Z||000000||V6pack||05-31-2000||08:20 PM||||Is it possible/practical to remove a front crossmember with complete suspension attached, from one Fiero and put it on another Fiero?  I have a re-sprung re-built front end I'd like to switch into another car in one fell swoop.  All help appreciated.<P>v6pack<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Raydar||05-31-2000||08:32 PM||||Yep. Except the 88s won't interchange with other years. There *may* be some differences with the 84, but I doubt it.||||reg||14
Z||000002||V6pack||05-31-2000||08:53 PM||||Thanks Raydar.  Are the 4 bolts(two each side) all that hold the crossmember to the underside of the space frame?  I could see no others along the crossmember, and of course all the manuals don't show them...just a lot of detail about taking off individual front suspension componants.<BR>Thanks,<BR>v6pack||||reg||14
Z||000003||DiggityDan||06-01-2000||01:59 AM||||There's the four bolts on the bottom side and then three on each side above the springs. Besides that, you need to take lose the steering column from the rack-and-pinion, detach the brake lines, and unbolt the sway bar from the frame. I did this about a month ago on mine when I was doing front end work. I just used a jack in the middle to lower it out, roll it out, and then replaced.||||reg||1
